      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>Mint with Tempest and Absolute Zero down.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Once I had Flesh of the Sun God out, I thought I'd draw the first side out to get a good setup by outracing the Baron's card destruction. But the environment and the non-fire damage (stupid Backlash Field) from the Baron took Tempest and Absolute Zero out. But then the game was&nbsp;pretty much locked. Tempest's incap power brought Ground Pound back into Haka's hand every turn (he had both copies available)&nbsp;and Absolute Zero's incap power destroyed any&nbsp;environment cards out so Haka's Domain would allow for lots of card drawing power every turn to fuel the Ground Pounds. With the environment and Baron Blade rendered helpless at that point, Ra blasted the Baron who could only stand there and watch the massive fireballs coming his way.</p>",
